# ANDROIDSERVICE — UI/UX VISUAL REMEDIATION PRD
## Version 3.0 — Senior-Level Production UI, Anti-AI-Slop & Visual System Overhaul

**Document type:** Product Requirements Document / UI Remediation Specification  
**Priority:** P0 — Visual quality and usability  
**Target:** Universal coding agents / OpenCode / CLI agents / AI coding assistants  
**Base product:** AndroidService — marketplace-style Android software service platform  
**Base requirements:** `android-service-marketplace-v2.prd`  
**Previous remediation:** `android-service-marketplace-ui-ux-fix-v2.1.prd`  
**Mandatory design skill:** `ui-ux-pro-max-skill` from `https://github.com/nextlevelbuilder/ui-ux-pro-max-skill`

---

# 1. PURPOSE

This PRD exists to correct the current visual implementation shown in the supplied UI screenshots and bring the website to a professional, production-grade standard comparable to work from a senior frontend engineer and senior product designer.

The existing implementation is structurally functional, but the screenshots reveal visual-system problems:

- Desktop and mobile navigation are not visually unified.
- Some navigation states appear too heavy or incorrectly sized.
- The service page contains excessive empty space and weak vertical rhythm.
- The search overlay/modal dominates the viewport without enough refinement.
- Some sections look unfinished or visually disconnected.
- The color system is overly pale and lacks a strong brand hierarchy.
- The dark remote-support section has insufficient text contrast.
- Typography hierarchy is inconsistent between sections.
- Cards and controls feel like generic template components.
- Large blank areas make the page feel unfinished.
- The overall UI currently risks an “AI-generated website” appearance.
- The design lacks enough distinctive product character.

The objective is NOT to add more decoration.

The objective is to create a coherent, restrained, trustworthy technical-service product UI.

---

# 2. NON-NEGOTIABLE DIRECTIVE

The coding agent MUST treat this PRD as an implementation specification, not as a loose design suggestion.

Before editing:

1. Read the base PRD.
2. Read this PRD completely.
3. Inspect the existing source code.
4. Inspect the existing design system.
5. Verify availability of `ui-ux-pro-max-skill`.
6. Perform root-cause analysis.
7. Create an implementation plan.
8. Then modify the UI.

Do NOT immediately rewrite the interface.

Do NOT blindly reproduce the screenshots.

The screenshots are evidence of problems, not a pixel-perfect target.

---

# 3. VISUAL REFERENCES ANALYZED

The provided screenshots show three important states:

## Reference A — Homepage desktop

Observed:

- Header is centered but visually undersized relative to the page.
- Hero content is too small relative to the available viewport.
- Hero has a large amount of unused vertical space.
- The dark problem-oriented panel is visually stronger than the actual primary CTA.
- Search field is visually understated despite being a core discovery feature.
- Category section begins too far below the hero.
- The page feels sparse rather than intentionally spacious.

## Reference B — Services page with search modal

Observed:

- Search modal is centered and functional but visually generic.
- Overlay darkens the entire page substantially.
- Modal width and header/input proportions need refinement.
- Popular-search chips look like generic pill UI.
- Background content becomes visually irrelevant rather than remaining contextually connected.
- Service cards have reasonable structure but insufficient visual differentiation.
- Cards use a repeated generic “icon + title + description + link” pattern.
- Category filter buttons are visually flat and do not strongly communicate active state.

## Reference C — Services page / mobile navigation state

Observed:

- Navigation expands into a large vertical list.
- The selected item uses a very large light-gray block.
- Navigation consumes excessive horizontal space.
- The visual relationship between navigation and page content is weak.
- The menu appears like an unstyled list rather than a designed navigation surface.
- There is excessive empty space around the navigation.
- The “Cari Layanan” CTA is too large and visually disconnected.
- Header/menu state lacks strong mobile information architecture.

These observations MUST be verified against the actual code before changes.

---

# 4. DESIGN DIRECTION

## 4.1 Product personality

The UI must communicate:

- Professional
- Technical
- Reliable
- Calm
- Clear
- Precise
- Human-operated service
- Modern Indonesian technology business

It should NOT communicate:

- Hacker culture
- Cyberpunk
- Gaming
- Crypto
- AI startup template
- Generic SaaS
- Cheap repair shop
- Shopee clone
- Lazada clone

---

# 5. ANTI-AI-SLOP REQUIREMENT

This is a mandatory quality gate.

The final website must NOT look like a website assembled from common AI-generated UI patterns.

## Explicitly avoid

- Huge gradient text.
- Purple/blue gradient backgrounds.
- Excessive glassmorphism.
- Excessive rounded cards.
- Every section inside a card.
- Excessive pill-shaped buttons.
- Random floating blobs.
- Decorative abstract shapes with no product purpose.
- Repeated “trusted by thousands” sections without real data.
- Fake review counts.
- Fake ratings.
- Fake customer numbers.
- Fake urgency.
- Fake countdown timers.
- Generic “AI-powered” visual language.
- Excessive use of icons as decoration.
- Emoji as UI icons.
- Excessive shadows.
- Excessive border radius.
- Excessive animations.
- Every heading containing a colored word.
- Identical card grids repeated throughout the page.
- Generic hero templates such as:
  “Transform your workflow with our powerful platform.”
- Stock-photo-style visual decoration with no relevance.

## Anti-slop principle

Prefer:

- Strong typography.
- Clear spacing.
- Intentional alignment.
- Real content.
- Real product hierarchy.
- Restrained color.
- Useful interaction.
- Meaningful visual differentiation.
- Consistent components.

A page with fewer elements but stronger hierarchy is preferable to a page filled with decorative UI.

---

# 6. BRAND COLOR SYSTEM

The current palette must be replaced/refined into a deliberate semantic system.

## 6.1 Recommended visual direction

Use a restrained:

**Ink / Off-white / Blue accent**

direction.

Suggested starting tokens:

```text
--background: #F8FAFC
--surface: #FFFFFF
--surface-subtle: #F1F5F9

--text-primary: #0F172A
--text-secondary: #475569
--text-muted: #64748B

--brand: #0877B5
--brand-hover: #06669C
--brand-active: #055A8A
--brand-subtle: #E8F4FB

--border: #E2E8F0
--border-strong: #CBD5E1

--dark-surface: #111827
--dark-surface-elevated: #1F2937
--dark-text: #F8FAFC
--dark-text-secondary: #CBD5E1

--success: #15803D
--warning: #B45309
--danger: #B91C1C
--info: #0369A1
```

These values are a starting direction, NOT permission to ignore the UI UX Pro Max design-system workflow.

The agent may adjust exact values after contrast and visual validation.

## 6.2 Color rules

Primary blue should be reserved for:

- Primary CTA.
- Important links.
- Active states.
- Search action.
- Important emphasis.
- Focus indicators where appropriate.

Do NOT make:

- Every heading blue.
- Every icon blue.
- Every card blue.
- Every border blue.

The blue accent must gain meaning through restraint.

---

# 7. TYPOGRAPHY

Typography must feel like a professional technology product.

## Requirements

Use one primary font family unless a second family is clearly justified.

Recommended characteristics:

- High legibility.
- Strong Indonesian language support.
- Excellent numeral rendering.
- Clear distinction between headings and body text.

## Type hierarchy

Define tokens for:

```text
display
h1
h2
h3
body-lg
body
body-sm
label
caption
```

Do NOT scatter arbitrary font sizes throughout components.

## Heading rules

H1 must be strong but not enormous.

Avoid:

```text
font-size: 72px
```

just because a large hero is fashionable.

The correct size is the size that produces a strong hierarchy while preserving useful content density.

## Body

Body copy should generally use:

- Comfortable line-height.
- 55–75 character readable measure where appropriate.
- Strong contrast.
- No excessive letter spacing.

---

# 8. LAYOUT SYSTEM

## 8.1 Container

Use a consistent content container.

Target:

```text
max-width: approximately 1120–1200px
```

The exact value must be determined by the design system.

Desktop content must not become excessively wide.

## 8.2 Alignment

The following should share consistent left/right alignment:

- Header content.
- Hero.
- Service grids.
- Section headings.
- Footer content.

Avoid independent container widths per section unless there is a clear reason.

---

# 9. HOMEPAGE REMEDIATION

## 9.1 Header

Desktop structure:

```text
[Logo]    Home  Layanan  Kategori  Cara Kerja  Remote Guide  FAQ          [Search]
```

Requirements:

- Header height approximately 64–72px.
- Logo vertically centered.
- Navigation vertically centered.
- Search icon aligned with navigation.
- Active page has subtle but clear state.
- No oversized empty header area.
- No unnecessary CTA in the header.

## 9.2 Header visual style

Use:

- White/off-white background.
- Thin bottom border.
- Minimal shadow only if required.
- Dark primary text.
- Blue active/hover indication.

Avoid a heavy floating-card header.

---

# 10. MOBILE NAVIGATION — COMPLETE REDESIGN

Mobile navigation is P0.

Preferred structure:

```text
[Logo]                              [Search] [Menu]
```

When menu opens:

```text
--------------------------------
[Logo]                          [X]

Home
Layanan
Kategori
Cara Kerja
Remote Guide
FAQ

--------------------------------
Cari layanan
--------------------------------
```

Requirements:

- Menu must feel intentional.
- Active item uses a subtle brand-tinted surface.
- Active state must NOT become a giant gray rectangle.
- Navigation rows should have consistent height.
- Touch target minimum 44px.
- Close control minimum 44px.
- No content clipping.
- No horizontal overflow.
- Menu should use proper z-index tokens.
- Background scroll must be handled correctly.
- Menu should have a clear visual boundary.

Recommended active state:

```text
background: brand-subtle
color: brand
font-weight: 600
```

Avoid:

```text
background: #E2E8F0
width: 100%
huge empty padding
```

unless the design system explicitly justifies it.

---

# 11. HERO REDESIGN

Current hero is too sparse.

Create a more deliberate two-column composition.

Recommended desktop:

```text
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                                                         │
│  eyebrow                                                │
│  H1 + supporting text            Problem selector       │
│  CTA                              / diagnostic panel     │
│  Search                                                  │
│                                                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

The right-side panel should feel like a useful product interaction, not merely a decorative dark card.

## Hero objectives

The user must understand within seconds:

1. What AndroidService does.
2. What problem it solves.
3. What services are available.
4. How to start a consultation.

## Avoid

- Giant empty vertical gaps.
- Excessive decorative elements.
- Huge heading that pushes everything below the fold.
- Multiple competing primary CTAs.

---

# 12. SEARCH EXPERIENCE

Search is a core product feature.

## Search button

The search trigger should be:

- Clearly interactive.
- Consistent with the brand.
- Not oversized.
- Accessible.

## Search modal

Use a refined dialog/sheet.

Structure:

```text
┌────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ 🔍  Cari layanan atau masalah...       X  │
├────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ Pencarian populer                          │
│                                            │
│ Bootloop   Root Android   Flash Firmware   │
│ Unlock Bootloader                          │
└────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

Requirements:

- Dialog must have accessible labeling.
- Close button must be clear.
- Focus must move into search input.
- Escape should close where appropriate.
- Background interaction must be blocked.
- Overlay opacity must be restrained.
- Modal should not feel detached from the product.
- Popular searches should use compact controls, not excessive pills.

---

# 13. SERVICE CATALOG REDESIGN

Current service cards are functional but generic.

Each service card should communicate:

- Service type.
- Problem solved.
- Availability/method if relevant.
- Clear next action.

Example hierarchy:

```text
[Icon]                         [Remote]
Root Android

Bantuan root untuk perangkat
Android yang kompatibel...

Persyaratan: ...
Metode: Remote

Lihat detail →
```

Do not add fake price if the service is quotation-based.

Do not add fake rating.

Do not add fake sales volume.

## Card rules

- Use subtle border.
- Very restrained radius.
- Minimal shadow.
- Clear hover state.
- Clear CTA.
- Consistent internal spacing.
- No nested card unless necessary.

---

# 14. CATEGORY FILTERS

Current category buttons are too flat.

Use a segmented/filter style with:

Default:

```text
background: surface
border: border
text: secondary
```

Active:

```text
background: brand
color: white
border: brand
```

Hover:

```text
background: brand-subtle
color: brand
```

Do not make every category a giant pill.

---

# 15. REMOTE SUPPORT SECTION

The dark section is a strong concept but currently has contrast/hierarchy problems.

## Required changes

Dark section:

- Use deep ink background.
- Heading must be high contrast.
- Body must use readable secondary contrast.
- Blue accent must remain visible.
- Buttons must have clear primary/secondary distinction.

Current problem:

Dark background combined with insufficiently contrasting heading/body makes the section visually muddy.

## Required hierarchy

```text
PREPARATION
Siap-siap untuk sesi remote support

Short explanation.

✓ PC/laptop
✓ Internet stabil
✓ AnyDesk resmi
✓ Ikuti arahan CS

[ Buka Remote Guide ] [ Download AnyDesk ]
```

Primary CTA should be visually obvious.

Secondary CTA should not compete.

---

# 16. SECTION SPACING

The current screenshots show excessive empty areas.

Do NOT simply reduce all padding globally.

Use a deliberate spacing scale.

Suggested:

```text
4
8
12
16
24
32
48
64
80
96
```

Large section spacing should be reserved for actual major transitions.

Avoid:

```text
hero padding: 160px
section padding: 160px
section padding: 160px
```

which produces a sparse, unfinished feeling.

---

# 17. PAGE DENSITY

Professional does not mean empty.

The UI should have enough content density to feel useful.

For the homepage, prioritize:

1. Hero
2. Search
3. Categories
4. Popular services
5. How it works
6. Remote preparation
7. FAQ
8. Final consultation CTA

Do not add unrelated marketing sections merely to fill whitespace.

---

# 18. ICONOGRAPHY

Use one icon family.

Requirements:

- Consistent stroke width.
- Consistent optical size.
- Consistent bounding box.
- No emoji.
- No random SVG styles.

Icons should support comprehension, not decorate every heading.

---

# 19. BUTTON SYSTEM

Create:

### Primary

For:

- Main conversion.
- Consultation.
- Important next action.

### Secondary

For:

- Supporting actions.

### Ghost/Text

For:

- Low-priority navigation.

### Icon button

For:

- Search.
- Menu.
- Close.

Every interactive control must have:

- Default.
- Hover.
- Active.
- Focus-visible.
- Disabled where applicable.

---

# 20. BORDER RADIUS

Avoid making everything a pill.

Recommended hierarchy:

```text
Buttons: medium radius
Inputs: medium radius
Cards: medium radius
Large panels: medium/large radius
Pills: reserved for tags/status only
```

Pills should NOT be the default shape for every control.

---

# 21. SHADOW SYSTEM

Use shadows sparingly.

Define:

```text
shadow-none
shadow-sm
shadow-md
```

Most cards should rely primarily on:

- Surface contrast.
- Border.
- Spacing.

Do not use strong shadows on every component.

---

# 22. RESPONSIVE REQUIREMENTS

Test:

```text
320px
375px
390px
768px
1024px
1280px
1440px
```

## Mobile

- Navigation must be stable.
- Search must fit.
- Hero columns become one column.
- Cards become one column.
- Buttons must remain tappable.
- No text clipping.
- No horizontal scroll.

## Tablet

- Avoid awkward two-column layouts.
- Maintain readable content widths.

## Desktop

- Use whitespace intentionally.
- Avoid stretching content across the entire viewport.
- Maintain strong alignment.

---

# 23. ACCESSIBILITY

Minimum requirements:

- Semantic HTML.
- Proper headings.
- Keyboard navigation.
- Visible focus.
- Accessible menu button.
- `aria-expanded` for expandable navigation.
- Appropriate `aria-controls`.
- Dialog semantics for search modal where applicable.
- Focus management.
- Escape-to-close where applicable.
- Color contrast.
- Reduced-motion support.

Do not remove browser focus indicators without replacement.

---

# 24. PERFORMANCE

Do not introduce visual libraries or animation libraries without justification.

Prefer:

- CSS transitions.
- Existing project utilities.
- Lightweight SVG icons.
- Optimized assets.

Avoid:

- Large animation packages for simple effects.
- Huge background images.
- Autoplay video.
- Unnecessary client-side rendering.

---

# 25. COMPONENT ARCHITECTURE

Shared components MUST be centralized.

Suggested:

```text
src/
  app/
  components/
    layout/
      Header
      MobileNavigation
      Footer

    ui/
      Button
      IconButton
      SearchInput
      SearchDialog
      Badge
      Card
      SectionHeading

    services/
      ServiceCard
      ServiceGrid
      ServiceFilters

    home/
      Hero
      ProblemPanel
      CategorySection
      RemoteSupportSection
      FAQPreview

  config/
    site
    navigation
    contact

  data/
    services
    categories

  lib/
    seo
    utils
```

Exact architecture may follow the existing project if it is already sound.

Do not duplicate components unnecessarily.

