Inspect:

- Existing UI.
- Screenshot-derived problems.
- Components.
- Tailwind/theme.
- CSS.
- Design tokens.
- Header.
- Search dialog.
- Service cards.
- Remote section.

Output an internal/root-cause report.

## PHASE 2 — DESIGN SYSTEM

Update `MASTER.md`.

## PHASE 3 — GLOBAL FOUNDATION

Fix:

- Colors.
- Typography.
- Container.
- Spacing.
- Radius.
- Shadows.
- Buttons.
- Inputs.

## PHASE 4 — NAVIGATION

Fix desktop and mobile navigation.

## PHASE 5 — HOMEPAGE

Refine:

- Hero.
- Search.
- Categories.
- Services.
- Remote section.
- FAQ.

## PHASE 6 — SERVICES

Refine:

- Search dialog.
- Filters.
- Service cards.
- Service detail.

## PHASE 7 — ALL OTHER PAGES

Ensure visual consistency.

## PHASE 8 — QA

Perform responsive/accessibility/anti-slop audit.

## PHASE 9 — BUILD

Run:

```text
type-check
lint
build
```

Fix all errors.

---

# 29. ROOT-CAUSE RULE

Before every visual fix, ask:

> Is this a component problem, token problem, layout problem, interaction problem, or content hierarchy problem?

Prefer fixing the shared cause.

Example:

BAD:

```text
Add margin-top: -12px to fix navbar.
```

GOOD:

```text
Inspect header height, sticky positioning, page offset,
stacking context, and navigation layout before correcting.
```

---

# 30. DO NOT REWRITE WORKING BUSINESS LOGIC

The remediation is primarily visual and UX.

Do not break:

- Service routing.
- Search behavior.
- Navigation routes.
- WhatsApp/Telegram links.
- AnyDesk links.
- Existing SEO metadata.
- Existing static service data.

If a component must be refactored, preserve behavior.

